{"title":"2023 WSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_WSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider acute triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is the orthocenter. Extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/3/bb3ddf9a5fa2fca5c4787d4f989af0eef1387bf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> to meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. The angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/6/1c63076818d68ae1e76f86099760783af1aae55d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ABH}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> meets the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93fb45572645dbe7adc88a1944400f44f6fc98ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=10, BH=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />, then the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/c/11c5ea5774a663fa2517dce85e6d24f66d60f0c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a\\sqrt{b}}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"35\" height=\"41\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is a squarefree positive integer and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_WSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/b/36b0310f24a304f780666a051da91d74fed00188.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(6mm); pair A = (10/sqrt(13),20*sqrt(39)/13); pair B = (0,0); pair C = (46*sqrt(13)/13,0); pair D = (10/sqrt(13),0); pair M = (10/sqrt(13),10*sqrt(39)/13); pair H = (10/sqrt(13),6*sqrt(39)/13); pair P = (575*sqrt(13)/338,345*sqrt(39)/338);  draw(A--B--C--cycle); draw(A--D); draw(B--P); draw(B--M,dashed);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, S); label(&quot;$M$&quot;, M, E); label(&quot;$H$&quot;, H, SE); label(&quot;$P$&quot;, P, NE);  dot(M); dot(H);  [/asy]\" width=\"408\" height=\"318\" /> </center><p> From the angle bisector theorem, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/a/a5ae2a07e9a78969949e92474c7acb4f55e2b468.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{AB}{AM} = \\frac{HB}{HM}\\implies\\frac{AM}{HM} = \\frac{AB}{HB} = \\frac{10}{4} = \\frac{5}{2}.\\]\" width=\"336\" height=\"37\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/6/e66a59766e56520ef16689fe5d9424de56f32598.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HM = 2a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/9/c292f51176fc6a0e13314bb2585bae1b1af75f61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM=5a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/d/c6da3602b617f5fd4d2ec1e56477ae50b4f62cac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AM = MD\\implies AM = MH+HD\\implies 5a=2a+HD\\implies HD = 3a.\\]\" width=\"567\" height=\"14\" /> From the Pythagorean Theorem on triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6adfd3ad27a2dddeb0af7131d73c33c86991e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5b0c84921ef190082fb61e5d3ca9297606d687c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HBD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/6/706a0380af39cac814c4b35daafeddd1594ccddd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BD = \\sqrt{AB^2-AD^2}=\\sqrt{100-100a^2}\\quad\\text{and}\\quad BD=\\sqrt{HB^2-HD^2}=\\sqrt{36-9a^2}.\\]\" width=\"636\" height=\"18\" /> So, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5e47ed1d7832b5596ee669df9fbfbc62d72cbd9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[100-100a^2=16-9a^2\\implies a^2=\\frac{12}{13},\\]\" width=\"300\" height=\"37\" /> meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/e/85e5edef0525192f7b400f827ed90030a231d41e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BD=\\sqrt{100-100a^2}=\\sqrt{100-100\\cdot\\frac{12}{13}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{100}{13}}=\\frac{10\\sqrt{13}}{13}.\\]\" width=\"473\" height=\"43\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/2/542af04c686893ea50d4b85ee09cdb0bc4665bed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle HBD\\sim\\triangle CBP\\sim\\triangle CAD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"232\" height=\"18\" />. Comparing ratios, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/1/35108b3a41aa8f60852ef079190ea00c28ad55d6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{BD}{HD} = \\frac{AD}{CD}\\implies\\frac{\\frac{10\\sqrt{13}}{13}}{3a}=\\frac{10a}{CD}\\implies CD=\\frac{30a^2}{\\frac{10\\sqrt{13}}{13}}=\\frac{36\\sqrt{13}}{13}.\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"53\" /> So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/5/c95da428ec4d5332eb7338de3a29bcf432a5f966.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BC=BD+DC=\\frac{10\\sqrt{13}}{13}+\\frac{36\\sqrt{13}}{13}=\\frac{46\\sqrt{13}}{13}\\quad\\text{and}\\quad AD=10a=10\\sqrt{\\frac{12}{13}}=\\frac{20\\sqrt{39}}{13}.\\]\" width=\"663\" height=\"43\" /> The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/0/87077505342d9e4b6669d11f71ea5ca42e75f764.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{BC\\cdot AD}{2}=\\frac{\\frac{46\\sqrt{13}}{13}\\cdot\\frac{20\\sqrt{39}}{13}}{2}=\\frac{460\\sqrt{3}}{13}\\implies 460+3+13=\\boxed{476}\\]\" width=\"489\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018024314\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.036 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 140/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7284/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:31901:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018024314 and revision id 274626. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}